IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ap-dates`
IMPORT `ap-duties`

-- Administration and Probate Act 1958 (Vic), Part IA (intestacy, ss 70A-70ZL), with the s 70M statutory legacy formula, the
-- s 3 legacy interest rate and the s 106 transitional rule.
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in ap-seat.l4, which imports it and never restates a rule.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Part's own words say no ("applies if", "is not entitled ...
-- unless", "does not apply if", a "means" definition); or NOTHING where the Part does not answer on the facts given, with a
-- "NOTHING-kind" comment. Amounts are in dollars. The Court's orders and the partners' agreements are inputs.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Administration
-- and Probate Act 1958, Version No. 130 (22 October 2025), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with
-- the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with
-- the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Part IA -- Intestacy`

§§ `s 106, s 70A -- when Part IA applies`

-- s 106(1): the amendments made by the Administration and Probate and Other Acts Amendment (Succession and Related Matters)
-- Act 2017, which inserted this Part IA, "apply in respect of the estate of any person who dies on or after the commencement
-- of the applicable amendment". The endnotes give the commencement as 1 November 2017 (No. 41/2017, "Ss 4-20 on 1.11.17").
`Part IA in this form commenced on` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 11 2017

DECLARE `What the person left` IS ONE OF
    `no will`
    `a will that does not effectively dispose of the whole estate`
    `a will that effectively disposes of the whole estate`

-- s 70A(1): "This Part applies if a person dies -- (a) without leaving a will; or (b) leaving a will which does not
-- effectively dispose of the person's estate wholly or partially." (2): with a will, it applies to the part not disposed of.
GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE
      `what the person left` IS A `What the person left`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70A -- Part IA applies` `the day of death` `what the person left` MEANS
    IF `the day of death` `is before` `Part IA in this form commenced on`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: s 106(1) leaves deaths before 1 November 2017 to the Part as it was before the 2017 amendments)
    ELSE CONSIDER `what the person left`
         WHEN `a will that effectively disposes of the whole estate` THEN JUST FALSE
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 70C -- surviving the intestate by 30 days`

DECLARE `Survival under s 70C` IS ONE OF
    `I survived the intestate by at least 30 days, so I may share`
    `I did not survive the intestate by 30 days, so I am taken to have predeceased`
    `30 days have not yet passed since the death`
    `the 30-day rule does not apply, because the estate would otherwise pass to the Crown`

-- s 70C(1): "A person is not entitled to participate in the distribution of an intestate's estate under this Part unless the
-- person survives the intestate for at least 30 days." (2): such a person "is taken to have predeceased the intestate" (see
-- finding 1). (3): "This section does not apply if its application would result in an intestate's estate passing to the
-- Crown". The days are counted from the day of the intestate's death (fork F3).
GIVEN `the day of the intestate's death` IS A DATE
      `the person has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person died` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
      `the estate would otherwise pass to the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Survival under s 70C`
`s 70C -- survival` `the day of the intestate's death` `the person has died` `the day the person died` `today` `the estate would otherwise pass to the Crown` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the estate would otherwise pass to the Crown` THEN `the 30-day rule does not apply, because the estate would otherwise pass to the Crown`
           IF `the person has died`
           THEN IF `the days from` `the day of the intestate's death` `to` `the day the person died` AT LEAST 30
                THEN `I survived the intestate by at least 30 days, so I may share`
                ELSE `I did not survive the intestate by 30 days, so I am taken to have predeceased`
           IF `the days from` `the day of the intestate's death` `to` `today` AT LEAST 30 THEN `I survived the intestate by at least 30 days, so I may share`
           OTHERWISE `30 days have not yet passed since the death`

§§ `Divisions 3, 5 and 6 -- who takes the residuary estate`

-- The family the intestate leaves, counted after s 70C (a person who did not survive 30 days is taken to have predeceased).
-- A "line" is a person who survives, or one who died before the intestate leaving someone who survives and takes their share
-- (ss 70L(3), 70ZB(3), 70ZG(2), 70ZI(3), 70ZK(3)).
DECLARE `The intestate's family` HAS
    `the number of partners` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of child lines` IS A NUMBER
    `some issue is not issue of a partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of parents` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of sibling lines` IS A NUMBER
    `a sibling's grandchild or remoter issue survives` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of grandparents` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of aunt and uncle lines` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Who takes the residuary estate` IS ONE OF
    `the partner takes the whole (s 70J)`
    `the partner takes the whole (s 70K)`
    `the partner takes the whole, as it is worth no more than the statutory legacy (s 70L(1)(a))`
    `the partner takes the chattels, the statutory legacy with interest and half the balance; the children's lines take the other half (s 70L(1)(b), (2), (3))`
    `the partners share the whole (s 70Z)`
    `the partners share the whole (s 70ZA)`
    `the partners share the whole, as it is worth no more than the statutory legacy (s 70ZB(1)(a), (b))`
    `the partners share the chattels, the statutory legacy with interest and half the balance; the children's lines take the other half (s 70ZB(1)(c), (2), (3))`
    `the children's lines take the whole (s 70ZG)`
    `the parents take the whole (s 70ZH)`
    `the siblings' lines take the whole (s 70ZI)`
    `the grandparents take the whole (s 70ZJ)`
    `the aunts' and uncles' lines take the whole (s 70ZK)`
    `the Crown takes the whole, though a sibling's remoter issue survives (s 70ZL; finding 2)`
    `the Crown takes the whole (s 70ZL)`

-- Division 3 (one partner): s 70J(1) "If an intestate does not leave a child or other issue but leaves a partner, the partner
-- is entitled to the whole"; s 70K(1) a partner and issue "who is also a child or other issue of that partner": the whole;
-- s 70L(1) a partner and issue "who is not the child or other issue of that partner": (a) the whole if the residuary estate
-- "is worth not more than the amount of the partner's statutory legacy", (b) otherwise the chattels, the legacy, interest and
-- "one half of the balance". Division 5 (more than one partner): ss 70Z (no issue), 70ZA (issue of one or more partners),
-- 70ZB (issue "not a child or other issue of any of those partners"). Division 6 (no partner, s 70ZF): children (s 70ZG),
-- parents (s 70ZH), siblings (s 70ZI), grandparents (s 70ZJ, "no sibling and no issue of a sibling"), aunts and uncles
-- (s 70ZK, the same bar), and the Crown (s 70ZL, "If no person is entitled").
GIVEN `the family` IS A `The intestate's family`
      `the residuary estate is worth` IS A NUMBER
      `the partner's statutory legacy` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Who takes the residuary estate`
`Part IA -- who takes the residuary estate` `the family` `the residuary estate is worth` `the partner's statutory legacy` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the family`'s `the number of partners` EQUALS 1
           THEN BRANCH IF `the family`'s `the number of child lines` LESS THAN 1 THEN `the partner takes the whole (s 70J)`
                       IF NOT `the family`'s `some issue is not issue of a partner` THEN `the partner takes the whole (s 70K)`
                       IF `the residuary estate is worth` AT MOST `the partner's statutory legacy` THEN `the partner takes the whole, as it is worth no more than the statutory legacy (s 70L(1)(a))`
                       OTHERWISE `the partner takes the chattels, the statutory legacy with interest and half the balance; the children's lines take the other half (s 70L(1)(b), (2), (3))`
           IF `the family`'s `the number of partners` GREATER THAN 1
           THEN BRANCH IF `the family`'s `the number of child lines` LESS THAN 1 THEN `the partners share the whole (s 70Z)`
                       IF NOT `the family`'s `some issue is not issue of a partner` THEN `the partners share the whole (s 70ZA)`
                       IF `the residuary estate is worth` AT MOST `the partner's statutory legacy` THEN `the partners share the whole, as it is worth no more than the statutory legacy (s 70ZB(1)(a), (b))`
                       OTHERWISE `the partners share the chattels, the statutory legacy with interest and half the balance; the children's lines take the other half (s 70ZB(1)(c), (2), (3))`
           IF `the family`'s `the number of child lines` AT LEAST 1 THEN `the children's lines take the whole (s 70ZG)`
           IF `the family`'s `the number of parents` AT LEAST 1 THEN `the parents take the whole (s 70ZH)`
           IF `the family`'s `the number of sibling lines` AT LEAST 1 THEN `the siblings' lines take the whole (s 70ZI)`
           IF `the family`'s `a sibling's grandchild or remoter issue survives` THEN `the Crown takes the whole, though a sibling's remoter issue survives (s 70ZL; finding 2)`
           IF `the family`'s `the number of grandparents` AT LEAST 1 THEN `the grandparents take the whole (s 70ZJ)`
           IF `the family`'s `the number of aunt and uncle lines` AT LEAST 1 THEN `the aunts' and uncles' lines take the whole (s 70ZK)`
           OTHERWISE `the Crown takes the whole (s 70ZL)`

§§ `ss 70J-70L, 70Z-70ZE -- what a partner takes`

DECLARE `A partner's entitlement` HAS
    `the whole residuary estate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the personal chattels, by value` IS A NUMBER
    `the statutory legacy` IS A NUMBER
    `interest on the statutory legacy at the legacy interest rate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the share of the balance` IS A NUMBER
    `the total, before interest` IS A NUMBER

-- What all the partners together take, before any division between several partners. In s 70L(1)(b) and s 70ZB(1)(c) the
-- chattels are taken out of the residuary estate's worth, then the statutory legacy, and "the balance" is what remains; where
-- the worth less the chattels is less than the legacy, the legacy is paid only to that extent (fork F4).
GIVEN `the family` IS A `The intestate's family`
      `the residuary estate is worth` IS A NUMBER
      `the personal chattels are worth` IS A NUMBER
      `the partner's statutory legacy` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `A partner's entitlement`
`Part IA -- what the partners take together` `the family` `the residuary estate is worth` `the personal chattels are worth` `the partner's statutory legacy` MEANS
    IF `the family`'s `the number of partners` LESS THAN 1
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: Divisions 3 and 5 speak only where the intestate leaves a partner)
    ELSE IF `the partners take the chattels, the legacy and half the balance`
         THEN JUST (`A partner's entitlement` WITH
                       `the whole residuary estate` IS FALSE
                       `the personal chattels, by value` IS `the personal chattels are worth`
                       `the statutory legacy` IS `the legacy paid`
                       `interest on the statutory legacy at the legacy interest rate` IS TRUE
                       `the share of the balance` IS `half the balance`
                       `the total, before interest` IS `the personal chattels are worth` PLUS `the legacy paid` PLUS `half the balance`)
         ELSE JUST (`A partner's entitlement` WITH
                       `the whole residuary estate` IS TRUE
                       `the personal chattels, by value` IS `the personal chattels are worth`
                       `the statutory legacy` IS 0
                       `interest on the statutory legacy at the legacy interest rate` IS FALSE
                       `the share of the balance` IS 0
                       `the total, before interest` IS `the residuary estate is worth`)
    WHERE
        `the class` MEANS `Part IA -- who takes the residuary estate` `the family` `the residuary estate is worth` `the partner's statutory legacy`
        `the partners take the chattels, the legacy and half the balance` MEANS
                `the class` EQUALS `the partner takes the chattels, the statutory legacy with interest and half the balance; the children's lines take the other half (s 70L(1)(b), (2), (3))`
             OR `the class` EQUALS `the partners share the chattels, the statutory legacy with interest and half the balance; the children's lines take the other half (s 70ZB(1)(c), (2), (3))`
        `the rest after the chattels` MEANS max 0 (`the residuary estate is worth` MINUS `the personal chattels are worth`)
        `the legacy paid` MEANS min `the partner's statutory legacy` `the rest after the chattels`
        `half the balance` MEANS (`the rest after the chattels` MINUS `the legacy paid`) DIVIDED BY 2

-- One partner: what the partners take together. Several partners: ss 70Z, 70ZA, 70ZB(1) share it "if there is a distribution
-- agreement, in shares in accordance with that agreement; or if there is a distribution order, in accordance with that order;
-- or in equal shares, in accordance with section 70ZE". The agreement's or the order's shares are not in the text (NOTHING).
GIVEN `the family` IS A `The intestate's family`
      `the residuary estate is worth` IS A NUMBER
      `the personal chattels are worth` IS A NUMBER
      `the partner's statutory legacy` IS A NUMBER
      `there is a distribution agreement or order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `A partner's entitlement`
`Part IA -- what I take as a partner` `the family` `the residuary estate is worth` `the personal chattels are worth` `the partner's statutory legacy` `there is a distribution agreement or order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Part IA -- what the partners take together` `the family` `the residuary estate is worth` `the personal chattels are worth` `the partner's statutory legacy`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: no partner)
    WHEN JUST e THEN
        IF `the family`'s `the number of partners` EQUALS 1
        THEN JUST e
        ELSE IF `there is a distribution agreement or order`
             THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: the distribution agreement or the Court's distribution order sets the shares)
             ELSE JUST (`A partner's entitlement` WITH
                           `the whole residuary estate` IS e's `the whole residuary estate`
                           `the personal chattels, by value` IS e's `the personal chattels, by value` DIVIDED BY `n`
                           `the statutory legacy` IS e's `the statutory legacy` DIVIDED BY `n`
                           `interest on the statutory legacy at the legacy interest rate` IS e's `interest on the statutory legacy at the legacy interest rate`
                           `the share of the balance` IS e's `the share of the balance` DIVIDED BY `n`
                           `the total, before interest` IS e's `the total, before interest` DIVIDED BY `n`)
    WHERE
        `n` MEANS `the family`'s `the number of partners`

§§ `ss 70L(2), (3), 70ZB(2), (3), 70ZG-70ZK -- what a relative takes`

DECLARE `My place in the family` IS ONE OF
    `a child, grandchild or remoter issue of the intestate`
    `a parent of the intestate`
    `a sibling of the intestate, or the child of a sibling who died`
    `a grandparent of the intestate`
    `an aunt or uncle of the intestate, or the child (cousin) of an aunt or uncle who died`

-- What the class of relatives takes together: "the other half of the balance" (ss 70L(2), 70ZB(2)) or the whole residuary
-- estate (ss 70ZG-70ZK); 0 where the class does not take.
GIVEN `the family` IS A `The intestate's family`
      `the residuary estate is worth` IS A NUMBER
      `the personal chattels are worth` IS A NUMBER
      `the partner's statutory legacy` IS A NUMBER
      `my place` IS A `My place in the family`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Part IA -- what my class takes together` `the family` `the residuary estate is worth` `the personal chattels are worth` `the partner's statutory legacy` `my place` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my place`
    WHEN `a child, grandchild or remoter issue of the intestate` THEN
        BRANCH IF `the class` EQUALS `the children's lines take the whole (s 70ZG)` THEN `the residuary estate is worth`
               IF    `the class` EQUALS `the partner takes the chattels, the statutory legacy with interest and half the balance; the children's lines take the other half (s 70L(1)(b), (2), (3))`
                  OR `the class` EQUALS `the partners share the chattels, the statutory legacy with interest and half the balance; the children's lines take the other half (s 70ZB(1)(c), (2), (3))`
               THEN CONSIDER `Part IA -- what the partners take together` `the family` `the residuary estate is worth` `the personal chattels are worth` `the partner's statutory legacy`
                    WHEN JUST e THEN e's `the share of the balance`
                    OTHERWISE 0
               OTHERWISE 0
    WHEN `a parent of the intestate` THEN `the whole if` `the parents take the whole (s 70ZH)`
    WHEN `a sibling of the intestate, or the child of a sibling who died` THEN `the whole if` `the siblings' lines take the whole (s 70ZI)`
    WHEN `a grandparent of the intestate` THEN `the whole if` `the grandparents take the whole (s 70ZJ)`
    WHEN `an aunt or uncle of the intestate, or the child (cousin) of an aunt or uncle who died` THEN `the whole if` `the aunts' and uncles' lines take the whole (s 70ZK)`
    WHERE
        `the class` MEANS `Part IA -- who takes the residuary estate` `the family` `the residuary estate is worth` `the partner's statutory legacy`
        GIVEN `the answer` IS A `Who takes the residuary estate`
        `the whole if` `the answer` MEANS IF `the class` EQUALS `the answer` THEN `the residuary estate is worth` ELSE 0

GIVEN `the family` IS A `The intestate's family`
      `my place` IS A `My place in the family`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Part IA -- the lines at the first level for` `the family` `my place` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my place`
    WHEN `a child, grandchild or remoter issue of the intestate` THEN `the family`'s `the number of child lines`
    WHEN `a parent of the intestate` THEN `the family`'s `the number of parents`
    WHEN `a sibling of the intestate, or the child of a sibling who died` THEN `the family`'s `the number of sibling lines`
    WHEN `a grandparent of the intestate` THEN `the family`'s `the number of grandparents`
    WHEN `an aunt or uncle of the intestate, or the child (cousin) of an aunt or uncle who died` THEN `the family`'s `the number of aunt and uncle lines`

-- How far down a share may pass: issue "and so on until the entitlement is exhausted" (ss 70L(3), 70ZB(3), 70ZG(2)); for
-- siblings and aunts and uncles one level only, to "a child who survives" (ss 70ZI(3), 70ZK(3)); parents and grandparents take
-- in their own right ("distributed equally between", ss 70ZH, 70ZJ).
GIVEN `my place` IS A `My place in the family`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Part IA -- the most levels below the first for` `my place` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my place`
    WHEN `a child, grandchild or remoter issue of the intestate` THEN 1000
    WHEN `a sibling of the intestate, or the child of a sibling who died` THEN 1
    WHEN `an aunt or uncle of the intestate, or the child (cousin) of an aunt or uncle who died` THEN 1
    OTHERWISE 0

-- My share: what my class takes, divided equally between the lines at the first level, and again between the lines in each
-- family below that, down to me ("in equal shares", "divided between that deceased child's children", "that child is
-- entitled to the sibling's share and, if there are 2 or more children, in equal shares").
GIVEN `the family` IS A `The intestate's family`
      `the residuary estate is worth` IS A NUMBER
      `the personal chattels are worth` IS A NUMBER
      `the partner's statutory legacy` IS A NUMBER
      `my place` IS A `My place in the family`
      `the lines further down my branch` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Part IA -- what I take as a relative` `the family` `the residuary estate is worth` `the personal chattels are worth` `the partner's statutory legacy` `my place` `the lines further down my branch` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the class amount` EQUALS 0 THEN JUST 0
           IF `the first level` LESS THAN 1 THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: the facts give no line for me at the first level)
           IF NOT (all (GIVEN k YIELD k AT LEAST 1) `the lines further down my branch`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: a family below the first level with no line in it)
           IF count `the lines further down my branch` GREATER THAN `Part IA -- the most levels below the first for` `my place`
           THEN JUST 0 -- the Part gives a share no further down this branch (ss 70ZH-70ZK); see finding 2
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the class amount` DIVIDED BY (`the first level` TIMES product `the lines further down my branch`))
    WHERE
        `the class amount` MEANS `Part IA -- what my class takes together` `the family` `the residuary estate is worth` `the personal chattels are worth` `the partner's statutory legacy` `my place`
        `the first level` MEANS `Part IA -- the lines at the first level for` `the family` `my place`

§§ `s 70M -- the partner's statutory legacy, and s 3 -- the legacy interest rate`

-- s 70M(1): "the amount of the partner's statutory legacy is $451 909". (2): for each later financial year, A x B / C (the
-- formula 58-6191a130-F2 in the .formulas.md sidecar), where A is $451 909 or, "if an amount has been calculated in
-- accordance with this formula and that amount is greater than $451 909, the amount as last calculated", B and C the
-- Melbourne all groups CPI for the latest reference period and a year earlier. (4): "if the amount of the variation is less
-- than $1000, it must be rounded to the nearest whole $1; and ... if ... $1000 or more, ... to the nearest whole $10". (3): a
-- reduced amount "does not take effect", and a later increase has effect only to the extent it exceeds the reduction (fork
-- F6: read as the amount in effect never falling).
`s 70M(1) -- the partner's statutory legacy` MEANS 451909

DECLARE `The statutory legacy for a year` HAS
    `the amount calculated` IS A NUMBER
    `the amount in effect` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the unit` IS A NUMBER, x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest` `the unit` `of` x MEANS
    IF x LESS THAN 0
    THEN 0 MINUS (FLOOR (((0 MINUS x) DIVIDED BY `the unit`) PLUS 0.5) TIMES `the unit`)
    ELSE FLOOR ((x DIVIDED BY `the unit`) PLUS 0.5) TIMES `the unit`

GIVEN `the amount last calculated` IS A NUMBER
      `the index B` IS A NUMBER
      `the index C` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount in effect last year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The statutory legacy for a year`
`s 70M(2)-(4) -- the partner's statutory legacy for the year` `the amount last calculated` `the index B` `the index C` `the amount in effect last year` MEANS
    `The statutory legacy for a year` WITH
        `the amount calculated` IS `the new amount`
        `the amount in effect` IS max `the amount in effect last year` `the new amount`
    WHERE
        `the A figure` MEANS max `s 70M(1) -- the partner's statutory legacy` `the amount last calculated`
        `the variation` MEANS ((`the A figure` TIMES `the index B`) DIVIDED BY `the index C`) MINUS `the A figure`
        `the rounded variation` MEANS
            IF (`the variation` LESS THAN 1000) AND (`the variation` GREATER THAN (0 MINUS 1000))
            THEN `rounded to the nearest` 1 `of` `the variation`
            ELSE `rounded to the nearest` 10 `of` `the variation`
        `the new amount` MEANS `the A figure` PLUS `the rounded variation`

-- s 3(1): "legacy interest rate means the rate that lies 2 per cent above the cash rate last published by the Reserve Bank of
-- Australia before 1 January in the calendar year in which interest begins to accrue". ss 70L(1)(b)(iii), 70ZB(1)(c)(ii):
-- interest "from the date of the death of the intestate to the date of payment of that legacy". Simple interest on a
-- 365-day year (fork F5).
GIVEN `the statutory legacy` IS A NUMBER
      `the cash rate` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of death` IS A DATE
      `the day of payment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 70L(1)(b)(iii) -- interest on the statutory legacy` `the statutory legacy` `the cash rate` `the day of death` `the day of payment` MEANS
    ((`the statutory legacy` TIMES (`the cash rate` PLUS 2)) DIVIDED BY 100) TIMES (max 0 (`the days from` `the day of death` `to` `the day of payment`) DIVIDED BY 365)

§§ `Division 4 -- the partner's property election (ss 70O-70W)`

-- s 70O: "(1) This Division applies if an intestate does not leave multiple partners. (2) This Division does not apply if
-- section 70J or 70K apply." It is the partner (s 70P) who may elect.
GIVEN `the family` IS A `The intestate's family`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70O -- I may make a partner's property election` `the family` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the family`'s `the number of partners` GREATER THAN 1 THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the family`'s `the number of partners` LESS THAN 1 THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 70P gives the election to the partner)
           IF `the family`'s `the number of child lines` LESS THAN 1 THEN JUST FALSE -- s 70J applies
           IF NOT `the family`'s `some issue is not issue of a partner` THEN JUST FALSE -- s 70K applies
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Last day for the election` IS ONE OF
    `the last day to elect is` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `three months from the date of the right to elect notice, once it is given`

-- s 70R(1): (a) a partner who is a personal representative: "within 3 months of the grant of administration"; (b) otherwise
-- "within 3 months of the date of the right to elect notice"; (c) "if the Court extends the time ..., by the date to which
-- the period for election is extended".
GIVEN `I am a personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
      `I have been given the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the notice` IS A DATE
      `the Court has extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the time is extended to` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Last day for the election`
`s 70R -- my last day to elect` `I am a personal representative` `the day of the grant` `I have been given the notice` `the date of the notice` `the Court has extended the time` `the date the time is extended to` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the Court has extended the time` THEN `the last day to elect is` `the date the time is extended to`
           IF `I am a personal representative` THEN `the last day to elect is` (`the date` 3 `months after` `the day of the grant`)
           IF `I have been given the notice` THEN `the last day to elect is` (`the date` 3 `months after` `the date of the notice`)
           OTHERWISE `three months from the date of the right to elect notice, once it is given`

-- Whether an election made (or to be made today) is in time, by the s 70R rule run from the day the period starts.
GIVEN `I am a personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
      `I have been given the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the notice` IS A DATE
      `the Court has extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the time is extended to` IS A DATE
      `I have made the election` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I made the election` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `What became of the step`
`s 70R -- what became of my election` `I am a personal representative` `the day of the grant` `I have been given the notice` `the date of the notice` `the Court has extended the time` `the date the time is extended to` `I have made the election` `the day I made the election` `today` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 70R -- my last day to elect` `I am a personal representative` `the day of the grant` `I have been given the notice` `the date of the notice` `the Court has extended the time` `the date the time is extended to`
    WHEN `the last day to elect is` `the last day` THEN
        JUST (`the outcome of` (`s 70R -- the partner must make the election in time` (`the days from` `the start` `to` `the last day`)) `by` `the claimant` `with` `make the partner's property election` `counted from` `the start` `done` `I have made the election` `on` `the day I made the election` `today`)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: the period has not begun, because no right to elect notice has been given)
    WHERE
        `the start` MEANS IF `I am a personal representative` THEN `the day of the grant` ELSE `the date of the notice`

DECLARE `The right to elect notice` IS ONE OF
    `the notice is due by` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `no notice is required, as I am the personal representative (s 70Q(3))`

-- s 70Q(1), (3): within 30 days of the grant of administration, unless the partner is the personal representative.
GIVEN `I am a personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The right to elect notice`
`s 70Q -- when I must be given the right to elect notice` `I am a personal representative` `the day of the grant` MEANS
    IF `I am a personal representative`
    THEN `no notice is required, as I am the personal representative (s 70Q(3))`
    ELSE `the notice is due by` (`the date` 30 `days after` `the day of the grant`)

GIVEN `the day of the grant` IS A DATE
      `the notice has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `What became of the step`
`s 70Q -- what became of the right to elect notice` `the day of the grant` `the notice has been given` `the day the notice was given` `today` MEANS
    `the outcome of` `s 70Q -- the personal representative must give the right to elect notice` `by` `the personal representative` `with` `give the partner the right to elect notice` `counted from` `the day of the grant` `done` `the notice has been given` `on` `the day the notice was given` `today`

DECLARE `What I must pay into the estate` HAS
    `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `the last day` IS A DATE

-- s 70W(1): the price is satisfied "first from money to which the partner is entitled from the intestate's estate" and then
-- from the partner's own money. (2): "(a) the partner's share of the residuary estate must be reduced by the price of the
-- property; and (b) if the price of the property is more than the amount of the partner's share of the residuary estate, the
-- partner must pay the difference into the intestate's estate before whichever of the following occurs first -- (i) the
-- distribution of the residuary estate; (ii) the end of 12 months after making the partner's property election." The last
-- day is the day before the distribution, where that is earlier (fork F7).
GIVEN `the price of the property` IS A NUMBER
      `my share of the residuary estate` IS A NUMBER
      `the day I made the election` IS A DATE
      `a day is set for the distribution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the distribution` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `What I must pay into the estate`
`s 70W(2) -- what I must pay into the estate, and by when` `the price of the property` `my share of the residuary estate` `the day I made the election` `a day is set for the distribution` `the day of the distribution` MEANS
    `What I must pay into the estate` WITH
        `the amount` IS max 0 (`the price of the property` MINUS `my share of the residuary estate`)
        `the last day` IS
            IF `a day is set for the distribution`
            THEN `the earlier of` (`the date` (0 MINUS 1) `days after` `the day of the distribution`) `and` `twelve months on`
            ELSE `twelve months on`
    WHERE
        `twelve months on` MEANS `the date` 12 `months after` `the day I made the election`
